    <briefdescription>
<para>Capped and/or floored floating-rate coupon. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The payoff <formula id="41">$ P $</formula> of a capped floating-rate coupon is: <formula id="42">\[ P = N \times T \times \min(a L + b, C). \]</formula> The payoff of a floored floating-rate coupon is: <formula id="43">\[ P = N \times T \times \max(a L + b, F). \]</formula> The payoff of a collared floating-rate coupon is: <formula id="44">\[ P = N \times T \times \min(\max(a L + b, F), C). \]</formula> <verbatim>  where \form#32 is the notional, \form#45 is the accrual
  time, \form#46 is the floating rate, \form#47 is its
  gearing, \form#48 is the spread, and \form#49 and \form#50
  the strikes.

  They can be decomposed in the following manner.
  Decomposition of a capped floating rate coupon:
</verbatim> <formula id="51">\[ R = \min(a L + b, C) = (a L + b) + \min(C - b - \xi |a| L, 0) \]</formula> where <formula id="52">$ \xi = sgn(a) $</formula>. Then: <formula id="53">\[ R = (a L + b) + |a| \min(\frac{C - b}{|a|} - \xi L, 0) \]</formula> </para>    </detaileddescription>
